From c03a5859e9e1429e3a26c22a86a5d5f8a863dea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:03:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: refuse B5G6R5 textures so they convert to
 RGBX8/RGBA8

The TPU decode of 16-bit packed colour formats reads back black on this hardware (R8/RG8 too,
which stay accepted and are a known limitation): a GL_RGB/UNSIGNED_SHORT_5_6_5 texture sampled
through the native driver returned black while zink returned the expected texels. Refuse
B5G6R5 for sampler bindings on top of the existing "formats the draw path can use" rule, so the
state tracker converts RGB565 textures to RGBX8/RGBA8 like it already does for RGB8.

That also fixes the handoff's mipmapped-non-renderable-format gap for this case: the converted
texture is a renderable 8888 format, so it gets the twiddled mip chain with GPU-generated levels
instead of keeping level 0 only.

Verified against zink: plain RGB565 sampling and a CPU-uploaded RGB565 mip chain (256x256,
9 levels, minified) both give identical sample checksums; the full gltri gate (49 mode runs)
passes; full native glmark2 0 errors, 0 MMU faults.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
index 1a11ccd7..42a03c49 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
@@ -93,9 +93,15 @@ pvr_is_format_supported(UNUSED struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
       return false;
 
    /* Only what the draw path can use, so the state tracker converts the rest (RGB8 textures to
-    * RGBX8, integer vertex attributes to float) instead of handing over formats it then rejects. */
-   if ((bindings & PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW) && !util_format_is_depth_or_stencil(format) &&
-       !pvr_draw_texture_format_supported(format))
+    * RGBX8, integer vertex attributes to float) instead of handing over formats it then rejects.
+    * B5G6R5 is refused explicitly on top of that: the TPU decode of 16-bit packed colour reads
+    * back black on this hardware, so the state tracker converts RGB565 textures to RGBX8/RGBA8
+    * instead (which also gives them working mip chains, since the converted target formats are
+    * twiddled with GPU-generated levels). R8/RG8 are left accepted but their TPU decode is
+    * unverified - a known limitation. */
+   if ((bindings & PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW) &&
+       (format == PIPE_FORMAT_B5G6R5_UNORM ||
+        (!util_format_is_depth_or_stencil(format) && !pvr_draw_texture_format_supported(format))))
       return false;
    if ((bindings & (PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET | PIPE_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET | PIPE_BIND_SCANOUT |
                     PIPE_BIND_SHARED)) &&
-- 
